.TH ZOOMRECTS 5 "October 2026" "Zoom Rects"
.SH NAME
zoomrects \- duration configuration for the Zoom Rects Omarchy plugin
.SH DESCRIPTION
Zoom Rects plays the classic Mac OS zoom-rectangle trail when a program
launch starts.
It then asks Omarchy to show its Launching box if that program's window
is not already on screen.
.PP
The box text from this plugin is
.BR Launching\[u2026] .
.PP
The watch mark is drawn only after this plugin has asked for that box, and
only while Omarchy's on-screen display reports open.
.PP
The trail runs from a 32\(mu32 rectangle to the focused screen's work
area.
That rectangle is centered on the pointer.
.PP
When the pointer position is unavailable, it is centered on the work
area instead.
If 32 pixels would not fit, the rectangle is made smaller so that it
stays inside the work area.
.PP
The work area is the focused monitor, inside that monitor's reserved
insets and its outer gaps
.RI ( general:gaps_out ).
.PP
The same trail plays in reverse when the window from that launch closes,
and only when the 32\(mu32 icon from the launch is still known.
.PP
The rectangles shrink from the window's latest rectangle to that icon.
When that rectangle was never seen, the trail starts from the work area
the launch grew into.
.PP
A window with no known icon does not play a close trail.
The watch and the Launching box are not part of the close.
.PP
After that load has finished, a later window of the same program is kept
invisible while the rectangles grow from the stored launch icon to that
window's own rectangle.
.PP
The window appears when the rectangles reach it, then shrinks back to the
icon when the window closes.
.PP
Toolbars, menus, tooltips, docks, splash screens, popups, and windows
attached to another window do not.
.PP
A window that maps while the load trail or the Launching box is still up
stays with that one load trail.
.PP
Later windows zoom unless
.B newWindows
is false.
.PP
The icon is stored when this shell sees the program launch.
A later window zooms only after that icon is stored.
.PP
The duration of the rectangle trail, and whether later windows zoom, have
defaults in the plugin code.
One optional file overrides those defaults.
It may set
.B durationSec
and
.BR newWindows .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zoomrects.json
Override file.
When
.I XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the file is
.IR $HOME/.config/zoomrects.json .
.IP
The file is JSON.
A missing file is not an error.
.IP
The plugin reads this file.
It does not create or rewrite it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B durationSec
Number of seconds requested for the unfilled rectangles to grow from
the 32\(mu32 rectangle described above to the focused screen's work
area.
.IP
The close trail uses this same duration to shrink from the window
back to that icon.
.IP
A later-window trail uses this same duration in both directions.
.RS
.TP
.B Default
0.1, from the plugin code, when the file is missing, unreadable, empty,
or not valid JSON, or when this key is absent or not a finite number.
.TP
.B Minimum
0.01.
A smaller finite number is raised to 0.01.
.TP
.B Maximum
0.5.
A larger finite number is lowered to 0.5.
.TP
.B On screen
The plugin divides the chosen time into 12 steps and rounds each step
to the nearest millisecond.
A step shorter than 1 millisecond becomes 1 millisecond.
The trail then lasts 12 times that step.
.IP
The default 0.1 lasts 96 milliseconds, in 8 millisecond steps.
.br
The minimum 0.01 lasts 12 milliseconds, in 1 millisecond steps.
.br
The maximum 0.5 lasts 504 milliseconds, in 42 millisecond steps.
.br
The example below, 0.05, lasts 48 milliseconds, in 4 millisecond steps.
.RE
.TP
.B newWindows
Whether a later non-toolbar window of a program that already played its
load trail zooms from the stored icon to that window, and back when the
window closes.
.RS
.TP
.B Default
true, from the plugin code, when the file is missing, unreadable, empty,
or not valid JSON, or when this key is absent or not a JSON boolean.
.TP
.B false
Only the load trail and its close play.
.TP
.B true
Later windows zoom as described above.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
{ "durationSec": 0.05, "newWindows": false }
.EE
.PP
Saving the file updates the step length and the later-window switch in
the running plugin.
The shell does not need to be restarted.
.PP
A trail that has already started keeps the outlines already drawn.
Later steps use the new length.
.PP
A later-window trail that has already started finishes.
The switch applies to the next window.
.SH SEE ALSO
The
.B README
in the plugin directory for install, update, and removal
.RB ( "omarchy plugin add" ,
.BR "omarchy plugin update" ,
.BR "omarchy plugin remove" ,
.BR "omarchy restart shell" ).
